{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_product_studio_census_gate", "label": "Studio Tool Census \u2014 the binding port acceptance gate", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/studio-census.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A merge gate for port PRs on par with typecheck and lint: every tool and computed output listed must survive the port, refactored to the design system and touch-first. The census never shrinks."}, {"id": "docs_product_studio_census_10_1_shell", "label": "10.1 \u2014 Studio shell, design list and Design Health", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/studio-census.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_product_studio_census_10_3_roof_setup", "label": "10.3 \u2014 Step 2 Roof setup (touch-first CAD, AI ghosts)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/studio-census.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "AI results arrive as ghosts to accept or reject, never applied silently, with per-shape confidence and dropped-shape warnings; relocating the pin >25 m wipes the design, kept as a clear undoable confirmation rather than a silent reset."}, {"id": "docs_product_studio_census_10_4_obstructions", "label": "10.4 \u2014 Step 3 Obstructions (11 types, nested bridging chain)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/studio-census.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_product_studio_census_10_5_components", "label": "10.5 \u2014 Step 4 Components (panel \u2192 capacity \u2192 inverter, compare)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/studio-census.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_product_studio_census_10_6_panel_layout", "label": "10.6 \u2014 Steps 5\u20136 Panel layout (the most tool-dense screen)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/studio-census.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Invalid electrical is a hard gate that blocks the next step with the reason stated; there is no subscription or plan-capacity limit anywhere, and flagging kWp over target stays a design cue."}, {"id": "docs_product_studio_census_10_7_3d_view", "label": "10.7 \u2014 The 3D view (sun, shadow, layers, in-scene editing, energy report)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/studio-census.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Neighbour buildings are decorative and must state plainly that they do NOT cast shadows; kWh/m\u00b2 carries the 'Real \u00b7 PVGIS' marker while geometric access numbers deliberately carry none."}, {"id": "docs_product_studio_census_10_8_proposal_captures", "label": "10.8 \u2014 Step 7 Proposal captures & readiness", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/studio-census.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A capture taken before a design change is stale and must say so, not silently show an out-of-date picture."}, {"id": "docs_product_studio_census_10_9_sld_drawings", "label": "10.9 \u2014 Step 8 SLD & drawings (four sheets, compliance check)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/studio-census.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The MAXIMUM SYSTEM VOLTAGE box must be prominent because it is the figure an electrical inspector checks; structural verification is a two-state human sign-off, never a computed adequacy claim."}, {"id": "docs_product_studio_census_10_10_bom_pricing", "label": "10.10 \u2014 Step 9 BOM & pricing (the ~286-control screen)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/studio-census.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Totals ARE the proposal money path \u2014 the same arithmetic the proposal uses, so it cannot produce a different total; each line's confidence tier and preliminary state travel onto the proposal's honesty labelling."}, {"id": "docs_product_studio_census_10_11_signoff", "label": "10.11 \u2014 Step 10 Done + engineer sign-off", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/studio-census.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The rule that does not bend: the app NEVER computes structural adequacy \u2014 it is a human decision recorded with who and when, and an unapproved design is never shown to the customer. Crew sees no money because the installation plan is a work order, not a quote."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_product_studio_census_gate", "target": "docs_product_studio_census_10_1_shell", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/product/studio-census.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_product_studio_census_gate", "target": "docs_product_studio_census_10_3_roof_setup", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/product/studio-census.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_product_studio_census_gate", "target": "docs_product_studio_census_10_4_obstructions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/product/studio-census.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_product_studio_census_gate", "target": "docs_product_studio_census_10_5_components",